.pytest_cache

# `*.json` above targets RUNTIME state (clusters/, replay_index.json, the
# legacy data/ tree). It also swept up two classes of file that are source,
# not state, and must survive a fresh clone:
#
#   1. Recorded contract fixtures. tests/acceptance/*/fixtures/*.json are the
#      captured vendor responses the parser is built against. Untracked, they
#      are absent on the VM after `git pull`, so the contract scenarios ERROR
#      instead of failing — the suite reports a problem with itself rather
#      than with the code.
#   2. nWave machine artifacts (roadmap.json, execution-log.json). DES reads
#      these to verify TDD phase compliance; an untracked audit log cannot be
#      audited by anyone but the machine that wrote it.
!tests/**/fixtures/*.json
!docs/feature/**/*.json
